`loc.js` is the headline "lines of code" metric, but its comment filter is line-by-line and misses `/* ... */` block comments whose continuation lines are not `*`-aligned. Those inner lines get counted as code.

The filter only strips lines that start with `//`, `#`, `/*`, `*`, or equal `*/`:

```js
.filter((l) => l && !l.startsWith('//') && !l.startsWith('#') && l !== '*/' && !l.startsWith('/*') && !l.startsWith('*')).length;
```

So a JSDoc-style comment (every line begins with `*`) is handled, but a plain indented block comment is not.

Repro:

```js
const loc = require('./benchmarks/loc.js');
const code = '```js
function f() {
  /* explain
     the rest */
  return 1;
}
```';
console.log(loc(code).score); // 5  (should be 3: function, return, closing brace)
```

The two comment lines ("the rest \*/" and the middle line) are counted as code. The same code written JSDoc-style scores 3 correctly, so the metric is inconsistent.

Impact: this over-counts LOC for any arm whose code carries plain block comments. Verbose baseline output tends to have more of them than ponytail's minimal output, so the bias runs in ponytail's favor on the headline "80-94% less code" number. It is small, but it is the kind of thing worth keeping honest.

Fix: strip `/* ... */` block comments before the line count. PR incoming with a regression test.

The SessionStart activation hook injects a statusline-setup nudge into Copilot CLI sessions, pointing at a Claude Code-only setting that does nothing for Copilot.

`ponytail-activate.js` gates the nudge with `if (!isCodex)`, which lets Copilot through:

```js
// hooks/ponytail-activate.js
if (!isCodex) try {
  ...
  if (!hasStatusline) {
    output += "STATUSLINE SETUP NEEDED: ... add this to ~/.claude/settings.json: " +
      statusLineSnippet + " Proactively offer to set this up for the user on first interaction.";
  }
}
```

The statusline badge is a Claude Code feature (configured in `~/.claude/settings.json`). Copilot CLI has no such statusline, so for every Copilot user without that file the hook tells the agent to *proactively offer* to edit a Claude Code settings file that is irrelevant to them.

Reproduced by running the hook under a Copilot env:

```
COPILOT_PLUGIN_DATA=/tmp/x PONYTAIL_DEFAULT_MODE=full node hooks/ponytail-activate.js
```

The emitted `additionalContext` contains `STATUSLINE SETUP NEEDED`, the `~/.claude/settings.json` snippet, and the "Proactively offer to set this up" instruction.

Codex is already excluded. Copilot should be too — the nudge only makes sense for Claude Code. Fix is to gate it with `if (!isCodex && !isCopilot)`. PR incoming.

